  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We treated HepG2 cells with a statin and harvested triplicates at 2, 8 and 24 hours, so 9 samples in total. The expression matrix is already log-transformed and centred per gene. I'd like a gene-gene co-expression network for each of the nine samples."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like a gene-gene co-expression network for each of the nine samples.\" -- available from LIONESS-COEXPRESSION.\n\nSeveral registered methods fit this result; they differ in their modeling assumptions:\n\n- **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. Needs expression matrix.\n- **BONOBO** — BONOBO applies Bayesian estimation and shrinkage to sample-specific gene-gene co-expression. Needs expression matrix.\n\nWhich modeling assumption best matches your experiment: Bayesian shrinkage; derive each sample network from all-sample and leave-one-out networks?\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
